1
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,266
Andaman, Andaman,

2
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:06,800
Andaman, Andaman,

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,133
Andaman, Andaman,

4
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:11,517
Andaman, Andaman,

5
00:00:11,517 --> 00:00:14,080
Andaman, Andaman.

6
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,266
Hey, sir!

7
00:00:33,266 --> 00:00:35,040
Sir!

8
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,240
Sir!

9
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,200
Sir! Sir!

10
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,720
<i>This is considered today's most shocking event.</i>

11
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:46,288
<i>Actor Anda, who made his debut
in a sensational series,</i>

12
00:00:46,288 --> 00:00:48,960
<i>was found dead inside a private vehicle.</i>

13
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,000
Authorities speculate that
stress from public criticism

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,920
may have been a contributing factor
that pushed him over the edge.

15
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:07,133
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

16
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:08,955
[are entirely fictitious.]

17
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:11,586
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

18
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:33,880
[One month earlier]

19
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,542
Podduang.

20
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:43,875
Podduang.

21
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,920
Podduang.

22
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,066
You're finally awake, Sleeping Beauty.

23
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:53,920
Or do I have to give you a kiss, too?

24
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,800
What the hell are you playing at?

25
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,822
You're sleeping like there's no tomorrow.

26
00:03:02,822 --> 00:03:04,080
Come on. Get up already.

27
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,133
How did you get in?

28
00:03:06,133 --> 00:03:07,440
What a question.

29
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,466
We were roommates for two years.

30
00:03:09,466 --> 00:03:11,280
In your third year, you moved to a condo.

31
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:14,200
Did you forget your ex already?

32
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:15,342
Come on!

33
00:03:18,355 --> 00:03:19,400
What is that sound?

34
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,111
The sound of hunger.

35
00:03:21,111 --> 00:03:22,253
Quick!

36
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:27,200
[Andaman]

37
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,920
[Fan Club]

38
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,280
[The Field of Love]
[Dorm Mate]

39
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,142
- Smells wonderful.
- Yeah.

40
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,200
I'm starving.

41
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,680
Bum.

42
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,644
What makes you this hungry?

43
00:03:49,644 --> 00:03:51,040
Well, last night,

44
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,120
a guitarist at my brother's place got sick,

45
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,800
so I was called in as a substitute until 3 a.m.

46
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,880
After I got up, Dunk dragged me here.

47
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,080
Why wouldn't I be hungry?

48
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:01,422
What? We have to make preparations, don't we?

49
00:04:01,422 --> 00:04:04,840
Orientation's almost over. I'm a third-year,
but they still don't know me.

50
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:08,240
We have to be the mean seniors, right?

51
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,222
We're on the entertainment team.

52
00:04:10,222 --> 00:04:13,533
So feel free to act all tough and cool
in front of the freshmen yourself.

53
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:15,511
I don't want them to hate me.

54
00:04:15,511 --> 00:04:17,480
They'll surely like me, right, Podduang?

55
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:20,040
- You're the most handsome.
- Absolutely.

56
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,964
Don't agree with him, Podduang.
Dunk is full of himself.

57
00:04:27,311 --> 00:04:28,755
Which one is better?

58
00:04:28,755 --> 00:04:30,040
Let me see.

59
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,764
- What are you doing?
- This one. This one.

60
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,480
It's about that Anda guy again?

61
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,680
Take that back!

62
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,760
How dare you address him like that?

63
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,960
What? My bad, all right?

64
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:44,831
Enjoy yourselves, you two. I'll go watch
the soccer highlights while I wait.

65
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,360
I'm so happy.

66
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:53,200
After two years of waiting,
Anda finally got cast as the lead pair.

67
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,680
Plus, he hits number one
on trending every week.

68
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,680
The agency must've acknowledged his potential.

69
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:00,040
Yeah, how fabulous.

70
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,760
You hyped up the trend, didn't you?

71
00:05:02,422 --> 00:05:04,480
- Nosy!
- Podduang!

72
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,760
- She said I'm being nosy.
- Well, you are.

73
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:10,600
<i>- It's absolutely red-hot right now,</i>
- Dunk, louder.

74
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:13,840
<i>- Anda and James's ship trend...</i>
- Dunk, stop!

75
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,880
What? What exactly do you want me to do?

76
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,680
We're telling you to stop!

77
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,080
<i>- Hello, James, Anda.</i>
- Don't switch the channel just yet.

78
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,577
<i>- Hi.
- Hello, hello.</i>

79
00:05:21,577 --> 00:05:25,133
<i>Is there anything you want to tell the fans
who are waiting for this series?</i>

80
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:27,520
<i>Anda, you go first.
Let me hold the mic for you.</i>

81
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:30,800
<i>Well, please look forward to it,
my lovely Andaman fandom.</i>

82
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,520
- Anda is so adorable.
- You're so right.

83
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,040
He's so cute in that look!

84
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:36,160
<i>- We put so much into this series.</i>
- Yeah, agreed.

85
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:37,680
<i>Yes, because...</i>

86
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:40,040
<i>this project has gone through
so much just to get here.</i>

87
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,240
<i>Everyone worked really hard.</i>

88
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,920
He's number one in my book.

89
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,040
Yeah, he's so cute.

90
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:48,520
<i>- Our first two series were well received.
- Yeah, yeah.</i>

91
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:51,160
<i>And I hope you're looking forward
to this one as well.</i>

92
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:54,600
So proud of him. My boy.

93
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:57,000
Come on. Let's prepare for the orientation.

94
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,840
[Welcome to
the Sports and Health Science Family]

95
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,000
[First Year]

96
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,933
[Ready to Roll]

97
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,875
Are you all having a good time here?

98
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,320
I guess not.

99
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:39,200
This year, the Faculty of Sports
and Health Science

100
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,240
has the lowest turnout for orientation.

101
00:06:43,088 --> 00:06:44,600
Why is that?

102
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,208
Where are all your friends?

103
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,542
Everyone, stand up!

104
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,520
Hey, quickly!

105
00:06:53,133 --> 00:06:55,120
Pick up the pace if you're one of us!

106
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:00,520
What I want to tell all of you is this:

107
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,680
We're all brothers and sisters

108
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,000
in this faculty.

109
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,520
We're one big family.

110
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,320
We truly mean it.

111
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:11,208
This means that

112
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,675
starting right now,

113
00:07:14,444 --> 00:07:16,186
I want everyone

114
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,160
to enjoy this moment with me.

115
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,560
Oh, come on.

116
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,280
You pulled off the act so seamlessly.

117
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,440
How come you couldn't tell?

118
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,040
- My outfit clearly gave it away.
- Dunk, Dunk.

119
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:34,225
Can I take a video of you? I'm going to shout,

120
00:07:34,225 --> 00:07:35,400
"Why are you wearing a suit, Boss?"

121
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,960
- Do a cool pose, okay?
- All right.

122
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,160
- Yeah, okay.
- Ready?

123
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,560
Three, two, one!

124
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,280
So...

125
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,280
Bum, my beautiful senior,

126
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:48,240
I want you to be my older sister
in the fraternity.

127
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,520
Should I be happy with the word "older"?

128
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:52,560
Oh, it was just a joke.

129
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,600
Podduang, can I have your autograph?

130
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,964
Absolutely.

131
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,186
Are you taken?

132
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:01,400
Wow.

133
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,160
"Are you taken?"

134
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,600
Right? Are you?

135
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:10,520
Like, is he usually this much of a goofball?

136
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,000
Always. It's his character.

137
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,640
All right. Everyone is here, correct?

138
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,880
Allow me to officially make
this announcement again.

139
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,560
A lot has changed nowadays.

140
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,200
This year's orientation requires
none of the drills

141
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,422
or the usual traditions.

142
00:08:27,422 --> 00:08:29,200
The seniors voted to make orientation

143
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,297
more about getting to know each other.

144
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,280
There's another thing you should know.

145
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:37,200
This year, there won't be

146
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,800
a Faculty Queen and King,

147
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,120
even though we used to have

148
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,760
our Faculty Queen

149
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,099
and our freaking Faculty King.

150
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,960
I think you two look like a couple.

151
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,240
Is there something going on?

152
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,400
Don't get flustered now.

153
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,240
Should we go back to the old way?

154
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:58,600
Right, right.

155
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,400
Let's get back on track.

156
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:03,320
Tomorrow night is the final day of orientation.

157
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:06,080
We want all of you here at 7 P.M. sharp.

158
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,480
We have something for you.

159
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,760
That's it for today.

160
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:23,080
[Kensan]

161
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,160
By the way, Podduang, how's your brother?

162
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:29,720
I heard he attended
the Faculty of Engineering orientation.

163
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,400
Satang didn't.

164
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:35,520
I think he has to go practice

165
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,760
with the youth squad.

166
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:38,297
He really is that good.

167
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,097
Don't you feel lonely living alone?

168
00:09:42,844 --> 00:09:45,560
Why? You're asking like
you want to move in or something.

169
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:48,320
I'd rather not. I'm afraid of heights.

170
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:52,440
Jeez, you've been with me since freshman year.

171
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,200
This is the first time you've told me.

172
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,040
What? Your old place was only four stories.

173
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,480
Your condo has way more floors.

174
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:02,240
Dunk, my room is on the third floor.

175
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:10,400
I know. I was just joking.

176
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,831
There, there.

177
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:14,160
Gosh, that tickles.

178
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,600
Here. I know it's your favorite.

179
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,520
Excellent. You know me so well.

180
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,920
Oh, Podduang.

181
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,533
Anda's filming for the faculty
this Saturday. Do you want to go?

182
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:32,600
Of course.

183
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:35,808
As members of the Andaman fandom,
we can't miss this.

184
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,875
Aren't you afraid to meet your bestie?

185
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:40,840
Who?

186
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,200
Jinna, obviously.

187
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,840
- Dunk, give it back to me.
- Hey, I was kidding!

188
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,320
- Give it back!
- I was joking.

189
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,160
- Come on!
- No, no. I'm sorry.

190
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:51,160
Why do you hate him this much?

191
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,280
Come on, Bum.

192
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,560
You forgot it all already?

193
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,600
Jinna and his friends always practiced
on our field when they were freshmen.

194
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,840
They never took care of the place either.

195
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:01,200
- And that guy always messed with me.
- Right.

196
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,760
Yeah, and he's always a poser.

197
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,080
Jinna or you?

198
00:11:07,688 --> 00:11:09,040
Jinna, of course!

199
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,475
I think it's you.

200
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,600
Hey, what's that?

201
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,986
Look.

202
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:17,840
Hey!

203
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,920
That's my meatball!

204
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,280
Please, please, please.

205
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,288
Hey!

206
00:11:22,288 --> 00:11:24,253
Hey. You can't have it.

207
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,440
Please.

208
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:29,760
- Hey!
- It's mine.

209
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,240
Hey, please.

210
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,560
Just one.

211
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,800
This one will do.

212
00:11:39,777 --> 00:11:41,000
I'm stuffed.

213
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,880
How are you getting back to your place?

214
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,080
I think I'm going to walk this way.

215
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:52,160
Yeah, same.

216
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,253
I'm going to stop by my brother's place first.

217
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,786
What about you?

218
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:02,360
I've called a ride. It should be here soon.

219
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,400
You two go ahead.

220
00:12:06,733 --> 00:12:09,920
Okay, I'll get going, then.

221
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,497
Yeah, get home safe.

222
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,360
Take care of the bill, okay?

223
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,480
Again, Dunk?

224
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:19,160
- See you.
- Bye-bye.

225
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,319
Bye-bye, Bum.

226
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,520
[Faculty of Engineering]

227
00:12:51,177 --> 00:12:52,853
Oh! I'm sorry.

228
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,897
The path is pretty wide.
Did you do that on purpose?

229
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,431
Who were you talking to?

230
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,497
Never mind.

231
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,160
- Do you know them yet?
- Got any alcohol?

232
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,960
- No, right?
- Introduce me to them.

233
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:36,960
Oh, it's our Faculty Queen and Faculty King.

234
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,120
- Took you forever.
- Good evening.

235
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,097
- Good evening.
- Podduang.

236
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,840
What took you so long?

237
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,920
Right, Golf.

238
00:13:56,920 --> 00:14:00,720
Nice. Nut.

239
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,560
Put your wristband on already. Come on.

240
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,280
- Jeez, I'm about to.
- It's on.

241
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,480
- Come on.
- You don't drink?

242
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:10,080
I do, but not alcohol.

243
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:12,120
I know...

244
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,960
you're having an after-party here.

245
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:18,266
Podduang, I know you've got
the slushy in your cup.

246
00:14:18,266 --> 00:14:20,640
These freshmen know too much.

247
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,160
How about a toast, man?

248
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:25,120
Not inviting your ship partner to sit with you?

249
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:29,520
Shit, if Bum hears you say that, you're dead.

250
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,640
Well, you two actually suit each other!

251
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,964
Bum, can you play a song for Dunk?

252
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,000
You're all pushing your luck tonight.

253
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,640
The Queen is coming.

254
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,942
- Things are about to go down.
- I'm scared.

255
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,080
Have a seat here.

256
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,400
This group... is pure trouble.

257
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:58,320
I'll have Dunk put you all on the soccer team.

258
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,200
Oh, bring it on!

259
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,942
- I'm the real deal. Just watch.
- The real deal.

260
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:07,600
You see, a newborn's first word is "mama,"
but for us, it's...

261
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:10,040
- "Goal!"
- "Goal!"

262
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,960
This batch of freshmen sure loves to brag!

263
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:15,735
Is it true that engineering students
are your rivals?

264
00:15:15,735 --> 00:15:17,415
Oh, there it is.

265
00:15:19,530 --> 00:15:21,480
What? Why are you looking at me?

266
00:15:22,835 --> 00:15:24,280
It's nothing, really.

267
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,360
When competing in sports,

268
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:28,560
the two faculties
always trade places between first and second.

269
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,600
So, who's first and who's second?

270
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,640
I'm first, of course!

271
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:35,280
- Oh, like we'd ever believe that!
- Expect us to buy that?

272
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,480
- For the likes of you--
- Hold on.

273
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,880
I'm your senior here.

274
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,880
Yes, Boss.

275
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:39,880
- Yes, Boss.
- Wait, wait.

276
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,920
- You're not wearing a suit tonight, Boss?
- Let's stop there.

277
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,840
I'm done with that bit.

278
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,740
Podduang, can you tell us

279
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,960
how the Faculty King and Queen contest went?

280
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:51,800
Hey, the Faculty King is right here.
Why not just ask him?

281
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,320
Scratch that!

282
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,906
Let's ask the Faculty Queen instead.

283
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,640
Why the hell do you even want to know?

284
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:00,153
You could've asked something else.

285
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,720
[Faculty of Sports and Health Science]

286
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,964
Are you in this section?

287
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,497
Yes. Are we in the same section?

288
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:33,400
I'm Podduang.

289
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,080
And I'm Dunk.

290
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,622
What a show-off.

291
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,755
Dunk is my name...

292
00:16:40,755 --> 00:16:42,231
And what's your name?

293
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,400
Bum.

294
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:45,800
You've got such a weird name.

295
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,560
Why the name "Podduang"?

296
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:50,240
Podduang was an ancient Thai currency.

297
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,480
Sheesh, that's dope!

298
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:54,387
I usually hear names like "Pound,"

299
00:16:54,387 --> 00:16:56,622
"Franc," "Euro," and "Dollar."

300
00:16:56,622 --> 00:16:58,600
The classics.

301
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,120
But...

302
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,400
you can just call me "Pod."

303
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,164
No, let's go with "Podduang." Sounds cute.

304
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,542
How about we...

305
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,742
sit together in the class?

306
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:18,760
Dunk, which bed do you want?

307
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,160
Any. You choose.

308
00:17:22,577 --> 00:17:23,880
I'll go with this one.

309
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,497
Okay.

310
00:17:26,111 --> 00:17:29,111
When will we get rid of
these aggressive orientation traditions?

311
00:17:29,111 --> 00:17:31,142
So fucking boring!

312
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:37,040
Well...

313
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,960
when you're in your third year,

314
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,160
try to become an aggressive senior yourself.

315
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,440
No way.

316
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,480
Even we gossip about them this much.

317
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:48,280
When I'm in my third year,

318
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:50,097
I won't be able to take it.

319
00:17:52,911 --> 00:17:54,385
What?

320
00:17:54,385 --> 00:17:56,364
- Why are you smiling?
- Nothing.

321
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,031
Dunk.

322
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,800
What's the matter?

323
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,511
You can't sleep?

324
00:18:24,511 --> 00:18:25,960
Yeah.

325
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:28,560
I'll get used to this place soon, I think.

326
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,586
I usually sleep with a bolster.

327
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,697
It's fine.

328
00:18:41,786 --> 00:18:44,581
I have two.

329
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:48,120
Thank you.

330
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,800
Sweet dreams.

331
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:51,320
- Good night.
- Let's sleep.

332
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,640
- Andaman!
- Andaman!

333
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,600
- This way.
- Come on, come on.

334
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:19,360
[Shine, Anda]
[Love Anda]

335
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:20,440
Thank you, thank you.

336
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,440
- Andaman!
- Andaman!

337
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,760
Andaman!

338
00:19:26,755 --> 00:19:30,920
- Who's that?
- Oh, that's Anda, a new actor,

339
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,444
and a first-year engineering student.

340
00:19:32,444 --> 00:19:33,520
He's so cute.

341
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:36,480
Jeez, you're not trying to hide it?

342
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,840
What does it have to do with you?

343
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,520
You're flustered. Podduang, look at her.

344
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,742
Hey!

345
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,520
Look at this.

346
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,560
Am I more handsome than him?

347
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:53,800
Not at all.

348
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:56,440
Not true. I'm more handsome.

349
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,240
- Andaman!
- Andaman!

350
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,880
- Right. Thank you.
- Andaman.

351
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,880
Those are our Faculty King and Queen!

352
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:33,120
- You two look so perfect.
- So cute.

353
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:34,440
Hey.

354
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,920
Doesn't her throat hurt when May yells at us?

355
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:41,320
Guys. I'm on a date now.

356
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:43,360
Whoa, with whom?

357
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:44,800
Golf, a third-year student.

358
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,720
Seriously?

359
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:48,920
I'm serious.

360
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:53,440
Hey. Come to think of it,
I think May is pretty cute.

361
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:58,560
Guys. I broke up with Golf.

362
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,400
Hey, it's okay.

363
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:02,240
You still have us.

364
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,720
- I'm on a date now.
- Congratulations.

365
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,720
Guys!

366
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,400
He told me I'm too manly for him.

367
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,520
I think he's wrong.

368
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,800
Damn it!

369
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,760
Why does it have to be me?

370
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,360
Burn the bridge. Trust me.

371
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:19,875
- I'm the one who has no time for him?
- Call it quits.

372
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:22,080
This guy's the one.

373
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,440
He's adorable!

374
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:26,320
Congratulations.

375
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,977
I already gave him a black eye.

376
00:21:28,977 --> 00:21:30,675
Great. Leave him.

377
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:34,831
Guys...

378
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:41,786
Look.

379
00:21:42,955 --> 00:21:44,742
Look at her pretending to be asleep.

380
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:48,960
Bum is living her life to the fullest?

381
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,942
Podduang.

382
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,520
Do you find Bum cute?

383
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:05,360
Are you saying...?

384
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:07,760
I don't know. Just forget it.

385
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:10,497
You sleep in my bed.
I'll sleep on the floor tonight.

386
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:55,208
What are you doing here all alone?

387
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:59,440
Isn't this the final day
of your faculty orientation?

388
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:02,080
I just want some peace.

389
00:23:03,044 --> 00:23:04,520
It's loud back there.

390
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:08,240
And why did you follow me here?

391
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:11,760
Did I? I was just jogging after practice.

392
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,631
Other people jog here, too.

393
00:23:15,755 --> 00:23:16,964
Can I sit with you?

394
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:27,440
Your faculty is very lively this year.

395
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,964
It's always been like this.

396
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:33,280
What's wrong?

397
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:35,160
You always look so upset.

398
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,697
I'm always like this.

399
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,942
You'd usually smile more.

400
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:47,200
You say that as if you're always with me.

401
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:50,964
Well, I do see you from time to time.

402
00:23:51,644 --> 00:23:55,364
I rarely get to see you outside Sports Day.

403
00:23:56,288 --> 00:23:57,440
Yeah.

404
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,120
Even back there,

405
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:03,400
